// Title: Persistence Via TypedPaths - CommandLine
// Sigma ID: ec88289a-7e1a-4cc3-8d18-bd1f60e4b9ba
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence
// Description: Detects modification addition to the 'TypedPaths' key in the user or admin registry via the
//   commandline. Which might indicate persistence attempt
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/dez_/status/1560101453150257154
//   - https://forensafe.com/blogs/typedpaths.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_registry_typed_paths_persistence.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Explorer\\TypedPaths"
